From 39b3c3beeedb7e37ca0bc591a4d376f4d1071243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:02:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] feat(windows): replace known-faulty libtool and gettext
 code

libtool's func_normal_abspath (2.2 through 2.6) takes only "/..." as an
absolute path.  Given a C:/ path it prepends the working directory and
never terminates; linking a DLL with -bindir reaches it, so libtool
hangs.  gettext's AM_PO_SUBDIRS code in config.status makes the same
assumption and writes ../C:/... paths into po/POTFILES, which breaks
the build of the po directories.

Every source tree and release tarball carries its own copy of this
code, so fixing it upstream does not help existing packages.  Recognize
the exact faulty function definitions and case command when they are
executed, and execute fixed versions instead.  Code is compared in its
printed form, which ignores comments and indentation, after a cheap
check of the function name or the case word.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
